    <string name="app_name">XingTe AntiLock</string>
    <string name="accessibility_desc">AntiLock accessibility service, used to pop up an uninstall list when locked by malware, helping to uninstall malicious apps.</string>
    <string name="main_title">AntiLock</string>
    <string name="main_info">1.Enable accessibility service by clicking the Accessibility Settings button. If denied, go to app details and tap the three dots in the top right corner to cancel, or join the QQ group for help.\n2.Activate and authorize Shizuku. If you don\'t know how, search for tutorials on Bilibili or join the QQ group.\n3.It is recommended to enable Force on Top. After AntiLock runs successfully, wait a moment, enable Force on Top, wait another moment, tap the wake button, and check if it works normally. If not, join the QQ group for help.\n4.AntiLock only reduces the risk of being locked. No tool can guarantee 100% security.\n5.AntiLock does not prevent factory reset or administrator lock (locking by changing your phone password).</string>
